 "_clips": "Joint angles in degrees (positive turns the part counter-clockwise as seen by the camera when the character faces right: a hanging arm or leg swings forward). root_y: metres the whole body rises. loop clips run on their own clock (length_s seconds, faster with the run speed when stride_scaled); the others are posed by how far through its action the character is (0..1). Single-key clips are held poses; the body blends into them. lean_bone takes the body's lean, scaled by lean_scale. A key may carry a third entry, the easing into it: in (accelerate, for a blow landing), out (decelerate, for a wind-up or overshoot), linear; default eases both ends. blend: how fast the body moves into the clip (per second, default 18). squash: positive coils the body down and wide, negative stretches it. secondary: bones that swing on their own from the body's movement (a spring: degrees per m/s forward and falling, limits, stiffness, damping). kicks: squash given on landing and on turning round (sprung, settles on its own). Story 054 (D-063): idle is a burdened stance (head bowed, shoulders loaded, a slow heavy breath); fall keeps the arms down and the knees ready, dragged rather than flailing. kicks.jump squashes the body for a push-off as it leaves the ground. Story 055 (D-066): dodge is a fast low step, not a roll: a dip, then a lunge sliding along the ground (front leg out, back knee down, cape trailing), held, then rising out of it. Story 057 (D-068): the combo is horizontal: attack_0 a forward cut swung from behind, attack_1 the backhand return, attack_2 a rising diagonal out of a crouch, attack_3 a wide spinning finisher; attack_air_0/1 cut with the legs tucked, attack_dash lunges out of a dodge, attack_up rises over the head. Every hit has a wind-up ('out'), a committed strike ('in') with a step and a weight shift, and a follow-through. Story 060: the run's arms swing against the legs again (sword arm +/-18, shield arm +/-8, the elbow pumping, the blade trailing) and the torso dips at each footfall; the earlier stiffness came from a doubled bob and a whole-body squash, both gone. Story 060: walk is a calm stride (legs and arms about half the run's); crouch is a low guard (knees deep, blade forward, shield up) with a slow breath; crouch_walk shuffles in it.",
